 lost Ukrainian friends\, Arsalan and Nastya\, as they reconnect in Germa
 ny after russia's full-scale invasion against Ukraine.  Arsalan\, an act
 or now in Frankfurt after time in a refugee camp\, and Nastya\, journali
 st and producer who stayed in Kyiv\, reflect on the divergent paths thei
 r lives have taken due to the war. Through their conversations and thera
 py sessions\, the film explores themes of displacement\, identity\, and 
 the emotional impact of war on youth.\n\nhttps://www.themoviedb.org/movi
 e/1559353
