SUMMARY:Borrowed from the Earth
DESCRIPTION:Directed by Zach Johaneson\n\nTells the story of the powerful
  connection between the Blackfeet people and horses\, and how that life-
 giving relationship remains alive today. Throughout their histories\, bo
 th horse and Indigenous people have been corralled - horses by fences\, 
 and Indigenous people onto reservations. Yet centuries-long attempts to 
 subdue both ultimately strengthened the bond between them. Saddle up for
  a visually poetic journey from the origin story of the horse to the mod
 ern day Indian Relay Race. Filmed on the Blackfeet Reservation in Browni
 ng\, Montana.\n\nhttps://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1776026
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1776026
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:movie-1700311@doc-radar
DTSTAMP:20261026T120350Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
SUMMARY:The Anti Expedition
DESCRIPTION:Directed by Elena Jean\n\nBob\, a young professor of outdoor 
 education\, was searching for an ethos to guide his teaching when he stu
 mbled upon a film made in 1971. The film depicted three mountaineers who
  chose not to summit a Himalayan mountain out of respect for local belie
 fs. For Bob\, it was this film\, and the work of Sigmund Kvaløy (one of
  the three mountaineers)\, that spurred a lifelong passion for ‘place 
 responsive’ outdoor adventure. In The Anti Expedition\, Bob and a team
  of seasoned adventure guides return the 1971 film to the Sherpa communi
 ty of the Rolwaling Valley. In a fascinating look at how five decades ha
 s affected both the valley and its people\, they rediscover that it's no
 t the destination that makes the journey meaningful.\n\nhttps://www.them
 oviedb.org/movie/1700311
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1700311
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
